# prefixsum

- Label: Prefix Sum
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 2
- Parameters: 4 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/prefixsum.html
- Summary (EN): The Prefix Sum node accumulates values across a layer's pixels along a chosen scan path. It combines values with addition, or tracks a running minimum, maximum or count.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Prefix Sum accumule les valeurs d'une couche le long d'un trajet de balayage, en addition, minimum, maximum ou comptage.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: original layer to compute the prefix sum from", "active (optional): per-pixel mask; values above 0.5 are included, values below 0.5 are excluded"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Direction: scan path: +X, -X, +Y, -Y, a meandering +X+Y path, or Linear (each horizontal line scanned before the next)", "Operation: Add, Minimum, Maximum or Count", "Scale: normalises non-integer sums by pixel size or by texture or image size; None disables scaling; the factor depends on whether the scan includes X, Y or both passes"]

- Caveats: ["Scale applies only to non-integer summation.", "With Image scale, a constant pixel value of 1 across the image sums to 2, not 1.", "The active input only affects which values enter the statistics."]

